    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="48">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:LeisWl">Leis Wl</ref> 48</head>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="xno" source="#robertson" n="48" corresp="#wit-i">Nuls ne receit hom[e] ultre III nuis, si [c]il ne li command od qui il fust ainz.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-i">No-one shall entertain a man for more than 3 days, unless he is committed to his charge by the man with whom he was formerly serving.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="519"><ref target="clause:IICn_28">II Cn 28</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 28</note>
        <note type="editorial">Added October 2026 from Robertson pp. 274–275 (text and translation); Liebermann’s text (K–M) not yet added</note>
      </div>
